# Consumables — heals and the one buff the README already promised.
#
# Heals are quoted in HEARTS (25 hp each, MAX_HEALTH 100 over four) so the
# numbers stay legible next to the King's Sword: a bandage is half a heart, stew
# is a full one. Both are made from things you trip over on the surface, which is
# the point — the deep tiers should be spent on picks, not on staying alive.
#
# "Abilities: ... fire damage protection" — that is the Emberward Draught. It
# carries no heal at all, only `use.effect fireward`, which is the contract name
# the buff system will look for.

@item bandage
name      Bandage
category  consumable
color     226 220 206
icon      icon_bandage
stack     20
tier      0
value     12
desc      Moss packed under cloth. Half a heart, no ceremony.
tags      food
use.heal  12
craft     in="sapling moss_clump" n="2 1" out=2 station=hand

@item mushroom_stew
name      Mushroom Stew
category  consumable
color     150 108 74
icon      icon_stew
stack     20
tier      1
value     34
desc      Boiled until the glow stops. A full heart, and it tastes of the caves.
tags      food
use.heal  25
craft     in="mushroom_cap sapling" n="2 1" out=1 station=furnace

@item emberward_draught
name      Emberward Draught
category  consumable
color     236 138 66
icon      icon_flask_fire
stack     10
tier      3
value     180
desc      Drink before the volcano, not during it.
tags      relic
use.heal      0
use.effect    fireward
use.duration  25
craft     in="gem crystal_shard ash_pile" n="1 2 2" out=1 station=workbench
# Repeating `craft` declares an ALTERNATE route, which is the whole reason the
# field is a record[]. An emberling's core is the cheap way in — if you can kill
# one, which is the trade.
craft     in="ember_core crystal_shard" n="1 2" out=2 station=workbench
